/-
Johnson/G/PackLit.lean: the lists of Johnson/G/PackFull.lean and Johnson/G/PackList.lean written out
as values, and the test of Johnson/Pack/Check.lean at every element, as theorems by an evaluation in
Lean's kernel.

`packFull` and `packSmall` are computed from public files by parsing, which Lean's kernel does not
evaluate. Here the same two lists stand as literals, written by program from Lean's own print of the
computed lists. Definitions, two theorems, and two tests by evaluation.
Whence the numbers: Lean's evaluator computed `packFull` from the three shipped public files
policy.txt, layout.txt and KL.bin of prover/examples/target_full_f2 (Johnson/G/KitFull.lean, with
their sums), and `packSmall` from the library's own copies of the three shipped public files of
prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy (OnBytes/Model/TestRecordWork.lean,
OnBytes/Params/SmallFiles.lean). No other file was read.
Main names:
  `packFullLit`, `packSmallLit`: for every sending of the seven plans, its chain's codes and its
    sampled messages' shapes, each with a radius.
  `packFullLit_meets`, `packSmallLit_meets`: `Johnson.Pack.allMeet` is true at every element.
The two tests: the literals are the computed lists.
Limits: the theorems speak of the literals. That the literals are what the planner of the verifier
on bytes gives at the public files is held by the two tests only: evidence by evaluation, with the
limits of Johnson/G/PackList.lean on the map from a message to its radius.
-/
